STEALTH RULES CHECKLIST

(If u follow this, bans become extremely rare)

I’ll split this into 7 layers.
If even one layer is sloppy → risk increases.

LAYER 1 — Account hygiene (before automation even starts)

Rule 1.1 — Account age

Never automate:

fresh accounts (<30 days)

accounts with <10 real interactions

Ideal:

90+ days old

profile filled

posts, likes, comments exist

Rule 1.2 — One account = one purpose

Never reuse:

same IG for multiple niches

same LI for multiple campaigns

Platform memory is long.

Rule 1.3 — Manual warm-up first
Before automation:

7–14 days manual usage:

scroll

like

view stories

send 1–2 real DMs/day

Automation should look like continuation, not start.

LAYER 2 — Identity binding (this is CRITICAL)

This is where most people screw up.

Rule 2.1 — Hard binding
Each account must be permanently bound to:

1 proxy IP

1 browser profile

1 Linkedin + 1 Instagram + 1 Facebook ! maximum

Hard rules for multi-platform in one browser

"Same IP for all 3

Same timezone

Same OS fingerprint

Same daily activity window

Never automate all 3 simultaneously

Switch platforms with idle time between"

1 user agent

1 timezone

1 OS fingerprint

Never mix.

Rule 2.2 — Sticky proxies only

Residential or mobile

Sticky session (24h+)

Never rotate mid-session / never rotate! 

Never change country/state

Rule 2.3 — Timezone must match IP
If:

IP = Texas

Browser timezone = UTC

❌ red flag.

LAYER 3 — Browser behavior (Playwright / Puppeteer rules)

Rule 3.1 — Headful > Headless

Use real browser mode

Headless = higher detection

Rule 3.2 — Human interaction simulation
Your browser MUST:

scroll pages

pause while loading

move mouse (not perfectly straight)

click with delays

sometimes do nothing

Humans are inefficient. Bots are efficient.

Rule 3.3 — Random but bounded delays
Never fixed delays.

Example:

view profile → wait 7–22s

scroll → pause → scroll

before DM → wait 15–45s

Rule 3.4 — Never jump
Do not:

open profile → DM instantly

open DM → paste text instantly

Sequence should feel like:

“looking → thinking → typing”

LAYER 4 — Volume & pacing (MOST IMPORTANT)

Rule 4.1 — Daily hard caps (per account)

Instagram:

profile visits: max 100/day

story views: max 100/day

DMs: max 50/day

LinkedIn:

profile views: 100/day

connection requests: 10–20/day

DMs: 10-15/day

Email:

5-100/day/domain

warm domain only

Rule 4.2 — Soft caps (recommended)
Always operate below max.

If user sets 30:

system aims for 25-30

only climbs if many dead leads

Rule 4.3 — No streaking
Never do:

same number every day

same time every day

Randomize:

start time

stop time

daily count

LAYER 5 — Content & messaging stealth

This is where bans are earned.

Rule 5.1 — No trigger words
Never include:

“automation”

“leads”

“ROI”

“guaranteed”

“rank #1”

 "expert”

Especially in first message.

Rule 5.2 — No links in first touch
Zero links.
Zero calendars.
Zero websites.

Link = trust threshold breach.

Rule 5.3 — Message uniqueness
Platform looks for:

sentence structure

punctuation

rhythm

Your AI MUST:

vary length

vary opener

vary CTA style

sometimes ask nothing

Rule 5.4 — Imperfect human writing
Perfect grammar = suspicious.

Allow:

short sentences

casual phrasing

light typos (rare)

lowercase sometimes

But never:

slang overload

repeated gimmicks

LAYER 6 — Engagement patterns (this saves accounts)

Rule 6.1 — Mixed intent behavior
Automation must include:

scrolling without action

story viewing without DM

profile view without message

Humans don’t always act.

Rule 6.2 — Delayed follow-ups
Never:

follow up in <24h

follow up same tone twice

Good pattern:

message → wait → soft bump → value add

Rule 6.3 — Stop on reply
Instant stop when:

user replies

even negative reply

Continuing = spam signal.

LAYER 7 — Failure detection & self-protection

Rule 7.1 — Early warning signs
If detected:
captcha
sudden login
DM limits
message failures

→ IMMEDIATE STOP for 48–72h

Rule 7.2 — Cooldown logic
System must:

pause account
lower volumes
resume slowly
Never “push through”.

Rule 7.3 — Account isolation
If one account flags:

do NOT touch others
no shared proxies
no shared sessions

ABSOLUTE NEVER-DO LIST (tattoo this)

❌ No mass scraping
❌ No identical messages
❌ No fresh accounts
❌ No proxy rotation mid-session
❌ No quota forcing
❌ No link in first DM(when u messaging first)
❌ No sudden behavior change

Break any one → risk multiplies.




Dead Account Scoring Logic (FULL)

This should be rules + score, not binary.

Goal

Decide:

Skip

Minimal touch

Normal outreach

Dead Score (0–100)
Platform signals

+40

Account not found / suspended

+30

Last post > 180 days

+25

Zero posts + zero bio info

+20

Private account + no highlights

+15

No profile photo / default avatar

+15

Website link dead or missing

+10

No bio description

+10

Followers < 50 (for businesses)

Email-specific

+50

Hard bounce

+30

Domain parked / no site

+20

Generic inbox (info@) + no site

Website signals

+30

Site offline / timeout

+20

Last update > 3 years

+15

No contact info

Classification
Score	Status	Action
0–29	Alive	Full outreach
30–49	Weak	Minimal / soft
50–69	Likely dead	Skip DM, maybe email
70+	Dead	Skip entirely

This logic is gold. It saves accounts.



Fingerprint tools (Multilogin-style logic)
Make each automated browser look like a real, unique human device (OS, screen size, fonts, timezone, etc.) so platforms don’t link multiple accounts together.

Canvas / WebGL spoofing
Hide the graphics fingerprint of the machine. Without this, sites like LinkedIn/Meta can detect that many accounts are coming from the same server, even if IPs change.